{{Navbar modding}}
{{Page version|42.18.0|2=984907}}
{{Removed|text=As of [[Build 42.13.0]], this feature is deprecated to only depend on [[translations]].}}
'''{{Code|DisplayName}}''' was used to set the display name of an item. This parameter was optional as of [[Build 42.12.3]]. It was suggested to use item name [[translations]] instead, which would take priority over this parameter. The priority order for the display name of an item was:
# [[Translations|Item name translation]] for current language
# [[Translations|Item name translation]] for English
# {{Code|DisplayName}} parameter
# Item full type

Below is an example usage of the parameter:
{{CodeSnip|code=
DisplayName = Opened Canned Tomato,
}}

{{Note|type=warn|It is highly advised to use translations instead of this parameter, as it provides other modders the ability to translate your items into their own language with simple addons for your mod.}}

== Using translation ==
{{Move|section=true|Item (scripts)|Item translation should now be explained in the main [[Item (scripts)]] page since the <code>DisplayName</code> parameter is now deprecated as of [[Build 42.13.0]].}}
Setup a [[Translations#Commonly used files|translation file]] for one or more languages inside the folder {{Code|media/lua/shared/Translate/{language code}/}} with {{Code|{language code}}} listed in the [[Translations#Languages|translations]] page. The file needs to be named {{Code|ItemName.json}}, which is case-insensitive:
{{CodeSnip|code=
media/
└── lua/
    └── shared/
        └── Translate/
            ├── EN/
            │   └── ItemName.json
            ├── FR/
            │   └── ItemName.json
            └── ...
}}

Inside the file, add a key-value pair for each item you want to translate, using the full type of the item as the key and the desired display name as the value. Make sure to include commas after each line item. A single line item and last line items do not require a trailing comma. This will cause a parsing error.

{{CodeSnip|code=
{
    Base.CannedTomato = "Opened Canned Tomato",
    Base.CannedCorn = "Opened Canned Corn"
<nowiki>}</nowiki>
}}

